-- title:
--   Valuation-ring points of uv = t^e lift to a chart
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring, $t \in W$ and $e$ a natural number with $0 < e$, and let $O$ be a commutative ring which is an integral domain and a valuation ring (for any two elements one divides the other). Write $\mathrm{CrossingQuotient}\ W\ s$ for the quotient of the polynomial ring $\mathrm{MvPolynomial}\ (\mathrm{Fin}\ 2)\ W$ in two variables $X_0, X_1$ over $W$ by the ideal generated by $X_0 X_1 - s$. Given any ring homomorphism $g \colon \mathrm{CrossingQuotient}\ W\ (t^e) \to O$, the assertion is that there exist an index $i \in \mathrm{Fin}\ e$ and a ring homomorphism $g' \colon \mathrm{CrossingQuotient}\ W\ t \to O$ such that composing the ring homomorphism underlying `resolutionChart t e i` with $g'$ gives back $g$. Here `resolutionChart t e i` is the $W$-algebra map $\mathrm{CrossingQuotient}\ W\ (t^e) \to \mathrm{CrossingQuotient}\ W\ t$ obtained from the universal property `lift`, sending the class of $X_0$ to $t^{i} u$ and the class of $X_1$ to $t^{\,e-1-i} v$, where $u, v$ denote the classes of $X_0, X_1$ in $\mathrm{CrossingQuotient}\ W\ t$; the required relation holds because $t^{i} u \cdot t^{\,e-1-i} v = t^{e-1} \cdot t = t^{e}$.
--
--   This is the pointwise form of the statement that the $e$ standard toric charts $\mathrm{Spec}\ W[x,y]/(xy-t)$ cover the resolution of the $A_{e-1}$-type singularity $uv = t^e$: it supplies the existence half of the valuative criterion of properness for that resolution, and is used in [`MvPolynomial.CrossingQuotient.Resolution.valuativeCriterion_existence_toCrossing`](thm.html#MvPolynomial.CrossingQuotient.Resolution.valuativeCriterion_existence_toCrossing).
